\section{Introduction}

To be written - notes and references so far

HHL \cite{harrow2009quantum}
Quantum Singular Value Transformation (QSVT)
\cite{martyn2021grand, gilyen2019quantum, dong2021efficient}
VQLS \cite{bravo2019variational} - NISQ

\cite{lapworth2022implicit} has shown the perfomance of HHL, relative to a classical linear
solver, must be assessed within the context of the convergence of the non-linear CFD solver.
For HHL, there is a specific iterative feed-forward mechanism associated with the 
under-resolution of the eigenvalue spectrum.
Similar behaviour is anticipated with other linear solvers, albeit as a result of different mechanisms.

